cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LabscribberPro in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LabscribberPro"
version: 1.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-27"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23689725
repository-code: "https://github.com/asifverse4/LabScribber"
abstract: >
  A browser-based, Electron-packaged scientific spectroscopy workstation
  covering UV-Vis, FTIR, Raman, 1H/13C NMR, 2D COSY, photoluminescence,
  XRD, XPS, cyclic voltammetry, EPR, and thermogravimetric simulation,
  with an automated test suite (177 tests, including UI-level tests)
  covering baseline correction, peak deconvolution with covariance-based
  uncertainty, Scherrer/Williamson-Hall XRD analysis, Tauc bandgap
  extraction, and a substantial chemometrics toolkit (PCA, MCR-ALS, PLS,
  hierarchical clustering).
authors:
  - family-names: Raza
    given-names: Asif
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3850-4907"
  - family-names: Basheer
    given-names: Huma
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6143-7192"
keywords:
  - spectroscopy
  - FTIR
  - Raman
  - UV-Vis
  - XPS
  - XRD
  - cyclic voltammetry
  - chemometrics
  - data analysis
  - scientific software
